From 44a053edd44812c0d0c881cbee94a85816da65e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pete O_o <pmb@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:54:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] systemd-target-monitor: add important services

Add an "important_services" list to the service monitor JSON. A failure
is logged and dumped like "services", but does not quiesce the BMC;
optional "start_units" are started instead.

```
"important_services": [
    "phosphor-ipmi-net@*.service",
    {
        "service": "phosphor-ipmi-host.service",
        "start_units": ["ipmid-recover.service"]
    }
]
```

The failure is logged at Error severity:

```
"message": "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Error.ImportantServiceFailure",
"severity": 3,
"additionalData": {
    "SYSTEMD_RESULT": "failed",
    "SYSTEMD_UNIT": "rsyslog.service"
}
```

Each failed start job is reported, so a service that systemd restarts
is logged (and its start_units run) once per failed attempt, not only
when systemd gives up on it.

Test Plan:
Flashed a yosemite4 image with this change. On the BMC, passed this
extra -s file to phosphor-systemd-target-monitor, with a test
important-fired.service that appends the date to
/run/openbmc/important-fired.

```
{"services": [], "important_services": [{"service": "rsyslog.service",
    "start_units": ["important-fired.service"]}]}
```

Then broke rsyslog:

```
mount --bind /bin/false /usr/sbin/rsyslogd
systemctl restart rsyslog.service

cat /run/openbmc/important-fired
Thu Oct 29 15:58:31 PDT 2026
Thu Oct 29 15:58:33 PDT 2026
Thu Oct 29 15:58:34 PDT 2026

busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC \
    /xyz/openbmc_project/state/bmc0 xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC \
    CurrentBMCState
s "xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC.BMCState.Ready"

curl -sk --cert $CERT --key $CERT \
    https://$BMC/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/3057
{
  "Id": "3057",
  "Message": "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Error.ImportantServiceFailure",
  "Severity": "Critical",
  ...
}
```

The BMC stayed Ready, start_units ran, and each failure was logged.

